WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
Recall our original four by four circulant Hadamard matrix.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.960
Its first row is negative one, one, one, one.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.800
Each following row is a right cyclic shift.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.300
Our goal is to replace the matrix by one algebraic object that

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.300
remembers all those shifts.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.940
Use the entries as polynomial coefficients.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:25.060
We get h of X equals negative one plus X plus X

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.240
squared plus X cubed.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.620
Work with the rule X to the fourth equals one, so the

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:31.740
powers wrap around.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.560
In dimension n, this is the integer group ring of the cyclic

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.720
group: integer polynomials modulo X to the n minus one.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:44.880
Its unique representative of degree less than n records the row unambiguously.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.060
Now multiply h by X.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.760
The last term becomes X to the fourth, which is one.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.925
The coefficients become one, negative one, one, one.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.380
That is exactly a right cyclic shift.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.560
Multiply by X again for the next row.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.080
Row j corresponds to X to the j minus one times h.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.220
After n shifts, the cycle returns to h.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.840
To encode dot products we need another operation: star.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.440
Replace X by X inverse.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.860
This fixes the constant coefficient and reverses the other cyclic positions.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:25.040
With generic coefficients, a, b, c, d becomes a, d, c, b.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:29.280
Our actual row is unchanged because its final three entries agree.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.620
Thus, for this example, h star equals h.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.660
Star reverses positions; it does not negate the coefficients.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.900
Multiply h by h star in this group ring.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:46.060
The coefficient at each power X to the a is the dot

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.900
product of the first row with its a step right shift.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.760
At the constant term we compare the row with itself: four squares

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:53.860
of signs give four.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:59.320
At X we get negative one, negative one, one, one, whose sum

00:01:59.320 --> 00:01:59.900
is zero.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.320
The two step and three step dot products are also zero.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.220
So every nonconstant coefficient vanishes.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.840
The whole product is simply four.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.700
One equation has encoded every orthogonality condition of our example.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:20.520
The same dictionary works in every dimension, provided all n coefficients are

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:21.720
positive or negative one.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:26.760
The matrix equation, H times H transpose equals n times the identity,

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.720
is equivalent to h times h star equals n in the group

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:30.940
ring.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.600
Forward, orthogonality makes the nonconstant coefficients zero, while the signs give constant

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.680
coefficient n.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:43.330
Conversely, the polynomial identity makes the first row orthogonal to every nontrivial

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:43.920
shift.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.120
Shift any pair of rows back together: their dot product becomes one

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:48.980
of those same correlations.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.080
Every distinct pair is therefore orthogonal.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.200
The sign hypothesis is essential.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:00.260
In dimension four, the constant polynomial two also has product four with

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:05.320
its star, but its coefficient row is two, zero, zero, zero.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.980
It gives twice the identity matrix, not a Hadamard matrix.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.860
With the sign hypothesis in place, the dictionary is exact.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.660
Explore the five smaller nodes for its ingredients.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.280
Next we use the identity to restrict the order n.
